# Testcase 14 — Resend from exported gap file
# Covers: REQ-3b, REQ-3d, REQ-40
#
# Workflow:
#   1. Normal upstream->downstream->dedup flow produces gaps (upstream's
#      deliverFilter=2,4,6 intentionally forwards only half the stream).
#   2. POST_DRAIN_SCRIPT (tc14-resend.sh) runs after the LG producer
#      finishes: `create` dumps those gaps as a JSON file, `resend` reads
#      it and reinjects the missing events via a fresh UDP sender —
#      exactly the manual procedure's two `docker compose --profile ...
#      run --rm ...` steps, but wired into the chain so it runs
#      automatically between "producer done" and "capture final verdict".
#   3. The sink's FINAL summary (captured after the post-drain hook) should
#      show all 100 events received with 0 missing — proving the gap-fill
#      actually closed the gaps, not just that gaps existed.
#
# Start with: ./run-testcase.sh 14            (full automated chain)
# Or run phases manually for inspection:
#   ./run-testcase.sh 14 -pause                (leave stack up)
#   docker compose --profile create run --rm create -- --resendFileName=/airgap/tmp/x.json --limit=all
#   docker compose --profile resend run --rm resend -- --resendFileName=/airgap/tmp/x.json

TC_TITLE="Resend: export gaps, replay via resend"
TC_COVERS="3b, 3d, 40"
TC_PROFILES="dedup"

UPSTREAM_A_CONFIG=/airgap/config/testcases/upstream-airgap-14-docker.properties
DOWNSTREAM_CONFIG=/airgap/config/testcases/downstream-airgap-14-docker.properties
DEDUP_ENV_FILE=../../config/testcases/dedup-14-docker.env
CREATE_CONFIG=/airgap/config/testcases/create-14.properties
RESEND_CONFIG=/airgap/config/testcases/resend-14.properties

# LogGenerator producer+sink.
LG_PRODUCER_CONFIG=/airgap/config/testcases/upstream-lg-14-docker.properties
LG_SINK_CONFIG=/airgap/config/testcases/downstream-lg-14.properties

# Dedup Kafka Streams needs 10-15s to finish REBALANCING before the first
# event lands — same race pattern as TC-9/10/12/13.
LG_STARTUP_DELAY=15

# Normal post-producer drain: gives dedup time to emit at least 2-3
# GAP_EMIT_INTERVAL_SEC=5 cycles BEFORE create runs, so the gap snapshot
# create exports reflects the complete (not partial) picture.
TC_DRAIN_SECONDS=15

# After the normal drain, run create -> resend -> propagation wait. See
# tests/env/tc14-resend.sh. TC14_RESEND_EPS throttles the UDP resend burst
# the same way eps=50 throttles the main upstream chain; without it the
# ~50 resent packets could hit the same burst-loss issue TC-9/10/12 hit.
POST_DRAIN_SCRIPT=tc14-resend.sh
TC14_BUNDLE_FILE=resend-14-all.json
TC14_PROPAGATION_WAIT=20
TC14_RESEND_EPS=50

# After resend fills every gap, the sink should see all 100 events with
# nothing missing — that's the whole point of TC-14.
EXPECTED_DUPLICATES=0
# After resend fills every detected gap, the sink should see ~100 events
# with (almost) nothing missing. "Almost" because of an inherent
# boundary effect of windowed gap-detection: a deliverFilter-dropped
# offset at the very TAIL of a partition's finite stream (nothing with
# a later, same-parity offset ever arrives to "close" the window) can
# never be proven a gap — create/resend literally can't see it, so it
# stays missing forever. With 100 events round-robined across 5
# partitions this costs at most a handful of events; observed 0-3 in
# practice. The range form absorbs that without masking an actual
# resend failure (which would leave ~45-50 missing, not 0-5).
EXPECTED_MISSING=0-5

# Prove dedup's own counters confirm the gaps actually closed (not just
# that the final count happens to look right). verify-tc14.sh checks for
# at least one negative delta_missing (a gap-closing event) and a final
# cycle with total_missing=0 across all partitions.
VERIFY_SCRIPT=verify-tc14.sh
TC14_PARTITION_COUNT=15
